Final: Dodgers win marathon 17-inning game in San Diego, 9-5 Share Pin It More Galleries Dodgers starting pitcher Kenta Maeda works against a San Diego Padres batter during the first inning on Sunday in San Diego. Gregory Bull, Associated Press Related article »
SAN DIEGO – The Dodgers needed a hero. It just took them a really long time to find one.
A really long time.
Yasiel Puig's two-run single in the 17th inning opened the door for a four-inning rally that sent the Dodgers to a 9-5 victory at Petco Park Sunday afternoon -- and evening -- and allowed them to avoid a three-game sweep by the San Diego Padres and end a four-game losing streak.
